   "evidence": "upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/PosDef.lean:62 `def PosSemidef (M : Matrix n n R) : Prop := M.IsHermitian \u2227 \u2200 x : n \u2192\u2080 R, 0 \u2264 x.sum fun i xi \u21a6 x.sum fun j xj \u21a6 star xi * M i j * xj` under `variable {m n R R' : Type*}` with no finiteness instance; EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/DataStructures/Matrix/PosSemidef.lean:87-99 `lemma PosSemidef.of_submatrix_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg`, docstring: \"A hermitian matrix over an arbitrary index type is positive semidefinite as soon as each of its principal submatrices on a finite family of indices (repeats allowed) has a nonnegative quadratic form. This is the arbitrary-index generalisation of `Matrix.PosSemidef.of_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg`\" \u2014 the PR uses the `Fintype`-bound `of_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg` at CovarianceMatrix.lean:125 instead.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Probability/Moments/CovarianceMatrix.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `[Finite \u03b9]` (keep `[IsFiniteMeasure \u03bc]` and `hX`) and prove it with the repo's `Matrix.PosSemidef.of_submatrix_dotProduct_mulVec_nonneg (isHermitian_covarianceMatrix X \u03bc) fun v c => ...`, rewriting the principal submatrix as `covarianceMatrix (X \u2218 v) \u03bc` via `covarianceMatrix_comp` and closing with `variance_dotProduct (fun k => hX (v k))` and `variance_nonneg` (`star c = c` over \u211d). This needs adding `public import EpsilonEridani.Mathematics.DataStructures.Matrix.PosSemidef`. Downstream `ofRandomVector` is unaffected, since `EuclideanDataset \u03b9` supplies `[Finite \u03b9]` itself.",
   "issue": "`posSemidef_covarianceMatrix [Finite \u03b9]` is stated for a finite index type, but positive semidefiniteness of a covariance matrix holds for an arbitrary `\u03b9`: `Matrix.PosSemidef` in pinned Mathlib quantifies over `x : n \u2192\u2080 R` and imposes no `Fintype`/`Finite` on `n`. The surrounding file is already index-type-free (`isHermitian_covarianceMatrix` line 89, `covarianceMatrix_comp` line 63), and its header advertises this as the general statement in which \"a finite covariance enters linear algebra as a `Matrix.PosSemidef`\", so the restriction is under-generalisation in exactly the file meant to be reusable.",
   "line": "122"
  }
